=product @PRODUCER@ @BASE@ VMSNOTIFY @PCSIVERSION@ full
1 'PRODUCER
=prompt @PRODUCER@
1 'PRODUCT
=prompt vmsnotify @VERSION@ for OpenVMS: operator log and audit journal to Gotify, Apprise, ntfy or a webhook
1 'NOTICE
=prompt vmsnotify is distributed under the MIT licence.
1 RELEASE_NOTES
=prompt Documentation is in [VMSNOTIFY.DOC]README.VMS under the installation directory.
1 POST_INSTALL
=prompt Post-installation tasks for vmsnotify
    Once, as SYSTEM: create the agent's account (default VMSNOTIFY, with
    a UIC group of its own above MAXSYSGROUP), set the protections, and
    create VMSNOTIFY$ROOT:[CONF]VMSNOTIFY.CONF from its example:
    $ @VMSNOTIFY$ROOT:[COM]VMSNOTIFY$CONFIGURE
    Set the endpoints in VMSNOTIFY$ROOT:[CONF]VMSNOTIFY.CONF and put
    their tokens in files in VMSNOTIFY$ROOT:[CONF] (token_file =), then:
    $ @VMSNOTIFY$ROOT:[COM]VMSNOTIFY_START
    At boot, add to SYS$MANAGER:SYSTARTUP_VMS.COM (after TCP/IP):
    $ @SYS$STARTUP:VMSNOTIFY$STARTUP.COM
    At shutdown, add to SYS$MANAGER:SYSHUTDWN.COM:
    $ @SYS$STARTUP:VMSNOTIFY$SHUTDOWN.COM

PRODUCT REMOVE VMSNOTIFY stops the agent and deassigns VMSNOTIFY$ROOT and
VMSNOTIFY$USER; the configuration, the tokens, the read position, the
logs and the account are kept.
